Subject: [mistral.rs] serve-request-path

  What a request carries into the chat template, and the one-line-in one-line-out record the serve lane keeps of it
  Two things a template needs and the message types did not hand it: tool call arguments as a map rather than a JSON string, and the assistant's own reasoning, which every vendor template renders back into history and no model could ever see, because neither the wire type nor the in-process message list declared a field for it
  Plus the ids the server advertises for the model it loaded, each naming the generation mode it serves, so a client pins a reference to what is loaded rather than a copy of it
  And the record says when a request produced NO ANSWER: a reply whose content channel is empty because the whole budget went to reasoning is indistinguishable from a refusal otherwise, and on the streamed path only a field carried across the chunks can tell them apart
  And the system message a chat that sends none is given: the embedder's default, installed once, so the model is told what it is
  And the phase the engine is in and the tokens it has sampled, read by the status line beside a server
  And a request for a model id the server does not serve is refused before it is parsed, with the status and the error object OpenAI gives it and one line saying which ids are served.

Applies to: 962112d18ea5729fe7acaae5085ce54c2fb66dab
